2.21.1.15 emacsvox-aural-editor-save
....................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-aural-editor-save

     Validate and atomically save or apply current working rules.

2.21.1.16 emacsvox-aural-editor-toggle-rule
...........................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-aural-editor-toggle-rule

     Enable or disable the selected working rule without discarding it.

2.21.1.17 emacsvox-aural-editor-validate
........................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-aural-editor-validate

     Validate all working rules and display diagnostics.

2.21.1.18 emacsvox-aural-scheme-editor-mode
...........................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-aural-scheme-editor-mode

     Accessible editor for declarative Presentation Options and rule layers.

     In addition to any hooks its parent mode
     ‘emacsvox-aural-interface-mode’ might have run, this mode runs the
     hook ‘emacsvox-aural-scheme-editor-mode-hook’, as the final or
     penultimate step during initialization.

     Key             Binding
     -----------------------------------------------------
     RET		emacsvox-aural-editor-edit-rule
     SPC		scroll-up-command
     -		negative-argument
     0 .. 9		digit-argument
     <		beginning-of-buffer
     >		end-of-buffer
     ?		emacsvox-aural-editor-help
     c		emacsvox-aural-editor-copy-rule
     d		emacsvox-aural-editor-delete-rule
     e		emacsvox-aural-editor-edit-rule
     g		emacsvox-aural-editor-refresh
     h		emacsvox-aural
     m		emacsvox-aural-editor-edit-metadata
     n		emacsvox-aural-editor-add-rule
     p		emacsvox-aural-editor-preview-rule
     q		emacsvox-aural-editor-quit
     t		emacsvox-aural-editor-toggle-rule
     v		emacsvox-aural-editor-validate
     w		emacsvox-aural-editor-save
     x		emacsvox-aural-editor-explain-rule
     DEL		scroll-down-command
     S-SPC		scroll-down-command
     M-<down>	emacsvox-aural-editor-move-rule-down
     M-<up>		emacsvox-aural-editor-move-rule-up

     C-c C-c		emacsvox-aural-editor-save

2.21.1.19 emacsvox-edit-aural-feature-fragment
..............................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-edit-aural-feature-fragment (&optional fragment)

     Open the declarative editor for personal feature FRAGMENT.

     (fn &optional FRAGMENT)

2.21.1.20 emacsvox-edit-aural-rules
...................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-edit-aural-rules (scope &optional fragment
          source-buffer)

     Open an accessible rule editor for SCOPE.

     SCOPE is ‘personal’, ‘session’, ‘buffer’, or ‘fragment’.  FRAGMENT identifies
     a personal Presentation Option.  SOURCE-BUFFER defaults to
     the ordinary source associated with the current buffer for buffer scope.
     Return the editor buffer.  Reopening a modified editor preserves its draft.

     (fn SCOPE &optional FRAGMENT SOURCE-BUFFER)


File: emacsvox-reference.info,  Node: emacsvox-aural-explanation,  Next: emacsvox-aural-feature-fragments,  Prev: emacsvox-aural-editor,  Up: Emacsvox Commands And Options

2.22 emacsvox-aural-explanation
===============================

Retained and simulated presentation explanations, spoken and visual
reports, spatial capability inspection, concise descriptions, and
training mode.

2.22.1 Emacsvox-Aural-Explanation Commands
------------------------------------------

2.22.1.1 emacsvox-aural-describe-spatial-capabilities
.....................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-aural-describe-spatial-capabilities

     Describe current spatial backends and user policy.

2.22.1.2 emacsvox-aural-explain-presentation
............................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-aural-explain-presentation (&optional facts
          context record)
     ‘C-e E’

     Explain exact queued RECORD or simulate FACTS in CONTEXT.

     Interactively, use the last queued presentation for the source buffer when
     available.  With a prefix argument, deliberately simulate an occasion chosen
     by the user.  When no queued record is available, infer the occasion that
     produces the most useful simulation.  The visual and spoken explanations
     always identify whether they describe queued output or a simulation.

     (fn &optional FACTS CONTEXT RECORD)

2.22.1.3 emacsvox-aural-training-mode
.....................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-aural-training-mode (&optional arg)

     Speak concise semantics after each normal aural presentation.

     This is a global minor mode.  If called interactively, toggle the
     ‘Emacsvox-Aural-Training mode’ mode.  If the prefix argument is
     positive, enable the mode, and if it is zero or negative, disable the
     mode.

     If called from Lisp, toggle the mode if ARG is ‘toggle’.  Enable the
     mode if ARG is nil, omitted, or is a positive number.  Disable the mode
     if ARG is a negative number.

     To check whether the minor mode is enabled in the current buffer,
     evaluate ‘(default-value 'emacsvox-aural-training-mode)’.

     The mode’s hook is called both when the mode is enabled and when it is
     disabled.

     (fn &optional ARG)

2.22.1.4 emacsvox-describe-aural-spatial-capabilities
.....................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-describe-aural-spatial-capabilities

     Describe current spatial backends and user policy.

2.22.1.5 emacsvox-explain-aural-presentation
............................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-explain-aural-presentation (&optional facts
          context record)

     Explain exact queued RECORD or simulate FACTS in CONTEXT.

     Interactively, use the last queued presentation for the source buffer when
     available.  With a prefix argument, deliberately simulate an occasion chosen
     by the user.  When no queued record is available, infer the occasion that
     produces the most useful simulation.  The visual and spoken explanations
     always identify whether they describe queued output or a simulation.

     (fn &optional FACTS CONTEXT RECORD)

2.22.2 emacsvox-aural-explanation Options
-----------------------------------------

 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-aural-training-mode
     Non-nil if Emacsvox-Aural-Training mode is enabled.
     See the ‘emacsvox-aural-training-mode’ command
     for a description of this minor mode.
     Setting this variable directly does not take effect;
     either customize it (see the info node ‘Easy Customization’)
     or call the function ‘emacsvox-aural-training-mode’.

     Default Value:

     nil


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-aural-training-mode-hook
     Hook run after entering or leaving ‘emacsvox-aural-training-mode’.
     No problems result if this variable is not bound.
     ‘add-hook’ automatically binds it.  (This is true for all hook variables.)

     Default Value:

     nil


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-aural-training-voice
     Palette-aware voice used for semantic training explanations.

     Default Value:

     annotate



